# Test authoring

Human contract: `docs/current/test-authoring.md`.
Landing card: `docs/history/card-plans/prep/测试制作流程详细计划.md`.

## Pick the layer

- Pure logic / data / JSON / counts → JUnit.
- Only real-world placement, capabilities, ticking → GameTest.
- Do not iterate hundreds of thousands of recipes inside a GameTest.

## Fixtures

- Use only parts GT6 registers and CC already registers. Check
  `gt6_code/gregtech6` and `python tools/gt6_resolve.py` first.
- No pure tin or iron pipes (GT6 has none). Non-gasproof pipe → wood /
  treated wood fluid pipe.
- Missing part = assertion failure. Never swap in another material, prefix,
  or vanilla item.
- Copy the material `ItemStack`; `new ItemStack(item)` drops components.

## Expected values

- GT6 source fact (blade count, energy side): may be literal; cite GT6 file:line.
- Projection of our own data (recipe / EMI / catalog counts): compare against
  runtime catalog or generated manifest. No new literal `== 12064`.
- Performance: separate budget assert. Never raise budget constants to go green.
- Changing a literal: state which data change caused it.

## GameTest must not throw

```java
// BAD
var be = (FooBlockEntity) helper.getBlockEntity(pos);
var r = map.findMatch(q).orElseThrow();
// GOOD
helper.assertTrue(helper.getBlockEntity(pos) instanceof FooBlockEntity, "missing Foo at " + pos);
var r = map.findMatch(q).orElse(null);
helper.assertTrue(r != null, "no match for " + q);
```

- `level.getCapability` needs `helper.absolutePos(pos)`.
- Failure text ≤ 900 chars (long text breaks shutdown save).
- Place machines by `Gt6SidedIo`: electrolyzer / centrifuge power from BOTTOM.

## Running

- `-PgameTestFilter` is diagnosis only; close on the full grid.
- Never treat `gametest_receipt.json` as PASS.
- Never delete tests, drop `required`, or skip failures.
